## Skills available

- **`/checkpoint`** — mid-session state snapshot to `~/.claude/checkpoints/<repo>/`. Use every ~50 turns in long sessions.
- **`/brief`** — expand a one-line task into the full briefing template. Use at the start of non-trivial work.
- **`/spec`** — interview-driven SPEC.md for ambiguous features. Hands off to a fresh session for execution.
- **`/review`** — spawn a fresh-context reviewer subagent against a recent change. Writer/reviewer pattern from multi-agent research. *User-invocable.* Note: the equivalent assistant-side path is to dispatch `subagent_type: "savant-reviewer"` via the `Agent` tool — Claude should self-dispatch reviewers on non-trivial changes without waiting for the user to type `/review`. The slash command is for *when the user wants to initiate review*; the Agent dispatch is for *when Claude judges review is warranted*.
- **`/recall`** — retrieve past session context from `~/.claude/checkpoints/`. Use at the start of a fresh session in any repo where you've previously taken checkpoints. **Implicit invocation:** bare *"resume"* or *"resume from here"* as turn-0 also triggers it. **Degrades gracefully:** default mode is filesystem listing; semantic search via a vector index is optional and not required.
- **`/team-loop`** — orchestrate the named-role multi-agent cascade (Product Owner → Architect + Developer parallel → Frontend Builder → optional UX critic). Pauses for user approval between phases. Use when a product needs structured planning + execution and the discovery material already exists. Dispatches `~/.claude/agents/{product-owner,architect,developer,frontend-builder,ux-critic,business-controller,domain-reviewer}.md` personas.

